tabelaVaricoceleAdultoL4C2:
Vessels appear enlarged at the inferior pole of the testis when the patient is evaluated in a standing position;
No enlargement is detected if the patient is examined in a supine position.
Reflux observed only under during the Valsalva maneuver.

tabelaVaricoceleAdultoL5C2:
 Vessels appear enlarged even when the patient is studied in a supine position;
The dilatation is more marked in the upright position and during the Valsalva maneuver.
Testicular hypotrophy is common at this stage.
